# Requests the turn retries: two HTTP 500s with the Gateway's error shape and
# then an answer (r*), then a second prompt the fake gateway has no turn for,
# so every request fails with a plain-text 500 (f*). The two products' backoffs
# differ (xfx: 250 ms, then 500 ms, three attempts; fx: about a second, growing,
# without end), so the snaps are at times that catch xfx's row and the README
# says which fx snap shows the same state.
gateway interrupt-retry.json
wait 2
type try it
key Enter
wait 0.15
snap r0.15
wait 0.3
snap r0.45
wait 0.6
snap r1.05
wait 1.5
snap r2.5
type second try
key Enter
wait 0.15
snap f0.15
wait 0.4
snap f0.55
wait 2
snap f2.5
snapfull end
gwlog
